  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This Latvian-inspired stranded hat is worked bottom-up in the round with two 10-round geometric border bands in stranded colourwork above a rib brim, fitting adult heads of 54 (56, 58) cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bottom-up construction is chosen because the geometric borders can be precisely positioned above the brim. Two border bands are worked with a 3-round plain section between them; the colourwork travels in stranded "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "float"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "float"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " technique -- both colours carried across every round. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " method handles the full circumference. About 80 g MC + 50 g CC of DK yarn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK-weight wool yarn, MC (natural white)",
              "qty": "80 g (approx. 175 m)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "DK-weight wool yarn, CC (rust red)",
              "qty": "50 g (approx. 110 m)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 8 / US 6)",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "3.5 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 9 / US 4) -- for brim",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch markers",
              "qty": "9 (1 BOR + 8 crown)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle and scissors",
              "qty": "1 each",
              "substitutions": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "22 sts x 30 rounds = 10 x 10 cm in stocking stitch on 4 mm needles, blocked. Stranded fabric is denser; swatch the colourwork chart and measure. At 23 sts per 10 cm the crown is 55 cm for size S."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Before you cast on, circle your size -- every count reads S (M, L)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast on"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on the 3.5 mm needle with MC, cast on 120 (120, 126) sts (multiple of 6 for chart repeat). Tail formula: tail_cm = (needle mm x stitch count) / 10 + 15. For size L on 3.5 mm: (3.5 x 126) / 10 + 15 = 59 cm; round up to 65 cm. Join without twisting, place BOR marker."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 10 rounds of 2 x 2 rib in MC. Switch to 4 mm needle. After the brim, you should have 120 (120, 126) stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "First border band"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join CC. Work the 10-round geometric border chart, repeating the 6-stitch repeat around the full circumference. Keep "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "float"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "floats"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " loose."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Plain section"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 3 rounds in MC only."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Second border band"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work the 10-round chart again. After the second band, you should have 120 (120, 126) stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body to crown"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Break CC. Continue in MC until hat measures 20 cm from cast-on."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown shaping"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place 8 markers dividing sts into 8 equal sections."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Decrease round 1: *k to 2 sts before marker, k2tog; repeat from * 8 times. 112 (112, 118) sts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: knit all."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Continue alternating until 32 sts, then every round until 8 sts remain."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After the final decrease round, you should have 8 stitches on the needle, ready to gather."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Top finish"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut yarn with 20 cm tail. Draw through all 8 sts, pull firmly, fasten on inside."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common faults"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Geometric borders puckering: floats are too short. The diagonal shifts in the Latvian pattern mean some floats span 4 stitches; spread those stitches particularly carefully before passing the float."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Two border bands not evenly spaced: the 3-round plain section between bands was missed or the transition row was counted incorrectly. Use a row counter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Colour dominance inconsistent between bands: hold the same colour in the same hand for both bands."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. Block over a bowl, opening the geometric pattern while damp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash cool, reshape and dry flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Bohus-inspired mini hat uses angora-blend yarn and purl-stitch colourwork for a distinctive Bohus look."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}